 "result_text": "I changed `scval.to_struct` in `stellar_sdk/scval.py` to sort its keys alphabetically. I haven't run the reproduction against the network or any tests.\n\nMy diagnosis is that Soroban rejects maps whose keys aren't in sorted order. Your XDR had the keys in insertion order: `source`, `asset`, `price`, `timestamp`. Struct fields should be sorted, which would give `asset`, `price`, `source`, `timestamp`. The RPC then failed with \"failed to convert ScVal to host value\". I inferred this from the XDR and didn't confirm it against the RPC, so it's the likely cause rather than a proven one.\n\n`to_map` still keeps whatever order you give it, so a hand-built map has to be sorted by the caller.",
